@meta
id: 20-14
title: The file knows its own name
chapter: 20
type: lesson
skills: register-named
par: 21
minutes: 3
vscode: right-click the tab, Copy Relative Path, paste
open: src/domain/order/order.provider.ts

@brief
Some registers you cannot write to. Vim fills them itself, and they are
there to be read. The first is `"%`: the name of the current file, with
the path you opened it by.

The documentation generator wants every source file to begin with a
comment naming its path from the repository root, in the form
`// File: src/domain/order/order.provider.ts`. Add that line to the top
of this file without typing the path.

@keys
| `"%p` | put the current file's path |
| `"#` | the alternate file's path |
| `O` | open a line above |

@hints
Open a line above the first import, type the comment prefix, leave
insert mode, then put the register.
--
After `Esc` the cursor sits on the last character you typed, the space,
and `p` puts after it.
--
`O// File: ` `Esc` `"%p`.

@solution
    O// File: <Esc> "%p :wq<Enter>

Eighteen keystrokes including the save, and the path — the part you
would get wrong — is the part you did not type. `%` is the same name you see in `:ls` and
`:file`, relative to the directory vim was started in, so it is only
the repo-root path when vim was started at the repo root. That is the
usual habit and a good one.

There are a handful of these read-only registers. `"#` is the alternate
file, the one `Ctrl-^` would take you to. `":`, `".` and `"/` hold the
last command, the last inserted text and the last search; they are the
next lesson. `:reg` shows them all together, and any of them can be put
with `p` or dropped into a command line, which is where `%` is most
often used.

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
// File: src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }
}
